":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-19","committee":"Council","time":"2.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-21","committee":"Audit, Compliance and Governance Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Panel - Local Government Reorganisation","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-23","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-25","committee":"Cabinet Housing Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-22","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Panel - Local Government Reorganisation","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-29","committee":"Cabinet Housing Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Joint Scrutiny Panel - Local Government Reorganisation","time":"6.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Cheltenham council to fall \u00a3563,000 short of minimum reserves by March","lead":"Cheltenham's general reserves are forecast to fall to \u00a3937,000 by 31 March 2027, leaving the council \u00a3563,000 below the level its Section 151 Officer, the chief finance officer, assesses as prudent. An \u00a3838,000 forecast overspend is the cause. At the same time, the council's capital programme \u2014 money spent on long-lived assets such as buildings \u2014 is being cut by 13.5%, from \u00a342.96m to \u00a337.1m. The National Cyber Innovation Centre at Golden Valley, budgeted at \u00a332.85m, is unaffected and now represents 89 per cent of the entire capital spending plan. Separately, the Housing Revenue Account, which manages council housing and is funded by rents, is forecast to overspend by \u00a3650,000, driven by \u00a3465,000 in lost rental income from vacant properties and \u00a3201,000 in additional borrowing costs from higher interest rates.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"Notification of Decisions of the Community Infrastructure Levy (CIL) Joint Committee - officer report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk/documents/s55064/55064.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Cheltenham Council reserves fall below safety level as savings plan falters","lead":"Cheltenham Council's financial reserves have fallen \u00a3563,000 below the level the council's chief finance officer considers necessary for financial resilience, the Cabinet heard this week. The council has budgeted a \u00a31.054m savings programme for the year, but delivered only \u00a3222,565. A further \u00a3375,000 of savings are at risk, while \u00a3456,185 remain unidentified. The Section 151 Officer assessed that General Balances of \u00a31.500m were prudent; the council now forecasts only \u00a3937,000 by March 2027. The council's budget monitoring report also warns of deeper structural problems: a \u00a3750,000 non-recurring staffing underspend is masking the true position, while borrowing costs \u00a3498,000 over budget\u2014a pressure expected to persist into next year. The council faces a pre-existing \u00a3491,785 savings requirement for 2027/28 with no identified solution.","iso":"2026-09-15","paper_title":"Notification of Decisions of the Community Infrastructure Levy (CIL) Joint Committee - officer report","paper_url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk/documents/s55064/55064.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Housing Revenue Account Capital Forecast, 31 August 2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk/documents/s55196/55196.pdf","headline":"Energy Efficiency programme delivering on schedule with full budget spend forecast","detail":"The Energy Efficiency & Sustainability Measures scheme for 2030 climate targets is budgeted and forecast at \u00a34.645m (100% delivery). This includes loft insulation, cavity wall insulation, external wall insulation, and heat pump installation.","category":"capital","matters":"Demonstrates that at least one major programme is on track to deliver. Shows progress on climate commitments and planned maintenance despite wider programme delivery issues.","figures":"\u00a34,645,000 budget = \u00a34,645,000 forecast (100% delivery)","quote":"Energy Efficiency & Other Sustainability Measures Improving the energy efficiency of the existing housing stock to meet the targets for 2030 - measures include the installation of top up loft insulation, cavity wall insulation, external wall insulation, and new heating systems such as ground source and air source heat pumps 4,645,000       4,645,000","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Housing Revenue Account Capital Forecast, 31 August 2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk/documents/s55196/55196.pdf","headline":"Lifts and Warden Call systems showing significant cost overruns","detail":"Two schemes show substantial cost increases: Lifts replacement (budgeted \u00a3300k, forecast \u00a3545.8k, overspend \u00a3245.8k or 82%) and Warden Call Upgrade (budgeted \u00a320k, forecast \u00a3145.8k, overspend \u00a3125.8k or 628%). The Warden Call overrun is particularly acute, suggesting major scope change or cost inflation.","category":"overspend","matters":"Cost pressures on these programmes indicate inflation, scope change, or unforeseen complexities affecting budget control. The Warden Call overrun (629% of budget) is material relative to the scheme's scale.","figures":"Lifts \u00a3300,000 \u2192 \u00a3545,800 (+82%); Warden Call \u00a320,000 \u2192 \u00a3145,848 (+628%)","quote":"Lifts Replacement of passenger lifts and installation of new chair lifts as required 300,000       545,800","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Housing Revenue Account Capital Forecast, 31 August 2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk/documents/s55196/55196.pdf","headline":"Kitchen improvements programme forecast to deliver only 41% of \u00a35m budget","detail":"The Kitchen Improvements scheme for internal refurbishment is budgeted at \u00a35m but forecast to spend only \u00a32.067m (58% underspend). This is the largest single scheme in the existing property improvements programme and represents substantial underperformance.","category":"capital","matters":"Significant underperformance on a flagship programme suggests contractor capacity, supply chain, or programme delivery management issues affecting the council's planned maintenance regime for existing stock.","figures":"\u00a35,000,000 budget \u2192 \u00a32,067,367 forecast (58% underspend)","quote":"Kitchen Improvements Kitchen Improvements 5,000,000       2,067,367","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Housing Revenue Account Capital Forecast, 31 August 2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk/documents/s55196/55196.pdf","headline":"Monkscroft School 70-home development only 48% forecast to be delivered","detail":"The Monkscroft School land-led scheme for 70 low carbon homes on council land is budgeted at \u00a38.58m but forecast at only \u00a34.15m (52% underspend). This major capital scheme represents one of the council's key housing developments and the shortfall indicates significant delay.","category":"capital","matters":"Delay in major housing development affects supply targets and demonstrates delivery capability concerns for a material scheme. The 52% underspend halfway through the year suggests the scheme may not meet its planned timescale.","figures":"\u00a38,580,000 budget \u2192 \u00a34,150,000 forecast (52% underspend)","quote":"Monkscroft School Land led scheme for 70 low carbon homes on Council land 8,580,000       4,150,000","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Housing Revenue Account Capital Forecast, 31 August 2026","paper_url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk/documents/s55196/55196.pdf","headline":"\u00a39.085m in acquisition schemes (S106 and Market Purchase) forecast to deliver zero spend","detail":"Two major acquisition schemes are both forecast at zero expenditure: S106 Purchases (\u00a34.085m for developer-led acquisitions) and Market Purchase (\u00a35m for local market acquisitions). These represent a complete stalling of acquisition activity despite being budgeted at mid-year.","category":"capital","matters":"Acquisition schemes are central to the council's housing strategy. Zero delivery represents a significant setback to planned housing supply and signals delays in scheme execution or approvals.","figures":"S106 Purchases \u00a34,085,000 \u2192 \u00a30; Market Purchase \u00a35,000,000 \u2192 \u00a30","quote":"Market Purchase Acquisition of individual properties from the local market to support the wider strategies within the HRA business plan 5,000,000       -","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-15"},"name":"Cheltenham","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-23","since_iso":"2026-08-24","distress":false,"headline":"Energy Efficiency programme delivering on schedule with full budget spend forecast","lead":"Demonstrates that at least one major programme is on track to deliver. Shows progress on climate commitments and planned maintenance despite wider programme delivery issues.","also":["16 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Cabinet Housing Committee on 2026-09-30","n_findings":17,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 3 - Housing Revenue Account Capital Forecast, 31 August 2026","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.cheltenham.gov.uk/documents/s55196/55196.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":71,"news_drafts_total":2}}